    4. For each wall segment bordering a chamber, place marker pixels to guarantee the chamber's chosen color wins by strict majority. Place markers only at non-intersection positions. Each marker must be on exactly one wall row or one wall col. Validate no ties.
    5. The output is the grid with chambers filled by their assigned colors.
    6. The input is the same grid but with chamber interiors set back to bg(0).
